        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1df01478-a8e5-59b9-a548-fdc700e1b245",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Baghdad ER, The Ten-Year Lunch: The Wit and Legend of the Algonquin Round Table\n- People: Matthew O'Neill, Jon Alpert, Dorothy Parker, Robert Benchley, George S. Kaufman, Edna Ferber, Marc Connelly, Harold Ross, Harpo Marx\n- Organizations: HBO, Algonquin Round Table\n- Places: New York City\n- Topics: Documentary films, Roaring Twenties\n\nFacts:\n- The Ten-Year Lunch: The Wit and Legend of the Algonquin Round Table is a 1987 American documentary film about the Algonquin Round Table.\n- The Algonquin Round Table was a floating group of writers and actors in New York City during the Roaring Twenties.\n- The Algonquin Round Table included Dorothy Parker, Robert Benchley, George S. Kaufman, Edna Ferber, Marc Connelly, Harold Ross, and Harpo Marx.\n- Baghdad ER is a documentary released by HBO on May 21, 2006.\n- Matthew O'Neill is a documentary filmmaker best known for his work on the HBO film Baghdad ER.\n- Matthew O'Neill and Jon Alpert won three Emmy Awards for Baghdad ER.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
